Linux Basics: The Ten-Step Trail
================================

Welcome. This short lab contains ten gentle checkpoints. Each flag is a marker
that you found the right clue; only checkpoint 10 is the final flag to submit.

Commands you will practise:
  ls -la, cd, cat, find, grep, base64, file, zcat, pwd, and basic permissions.

Checkpoint 1 is in this directory, but normal `ls` will not show it. Look for
hidden files, read the clue, and follow the trail one stage at a time.

Do not edit lab files. All content is readable with your generated SSH account.
